# Accepted gap: an ANONYMOUS CLASS has no constructor to point at. JLS 15.9.5.1 gives it an
# "anonymous constructor" that is implicitly declared and cannot be written, so the extractor emits
# no method entity for it — unlike a named class declaring none, whose implicit default constructor
# IS emitted and now resolves. Bytecode names the anonymous class's own constructor as the target of
# `new Iface(){...}`, so the edge is real; nothing in the IR can be its callee.
# It cannot rot: if the extractor starts emitting one, this line reports NOW-FIXED and fails.
testcases.engine.EdgeCHA#<init> -> testcases.engine.EdgeCHA$anon:Sink#<init>
